Here’s a compact console‑app that shows the different ways C# properties can be used:

```csharp
//  PropertyDemo.cs
using System;

namespace PropertyDemo
{
    // A simple class that exposes several kinds of properties
    public class Person
    {
        // 1. Auto‑implemented property (public get/set)
        public string FirstName { get; set; }

        // 2. Auto‑implemented property with a private setter
        public string LastName { get; private set; }

        // 3. Property that uses a backing field and validates input
        private int _age;
        public int Age
        {
            get => _age;
            set
            {
                if (value < 0)
                    throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(nameof(Age), "Age cannot be negative.");
                _age = value;
            }
        }

        // 4. Read‑only computed property (expression‑bodied)
        public string FullName => $"{FirstName} {LastName}";

        // Constructor
        public Person(string firstName, string lastName, int age)
        {
            FirstName = firstName;
            LastName  = lastName;
            Age       = age;
        }
    }

    // Demo program
    class Program
    {
        static void Main()
        {
            var p = new Person("John", "Doe", 30);

            Console.WriteLine($"Name: {p.FullName}, Age: {p.Age}");

            // Updating the age – valid
            p.Age = 31;
            Console.WriteLine($"Updated Age: {p.Age}");

            // Trying to change LastName (private set) causes a compile‑time error
            // p.LastName = "Smith";   // ← ❌ cannot assign to 'LastName' because it is read‑only

            // Setting a negative age triggers the validation logic
            try
            {
                p.Age = -5;
            }
            catch (ArgumentOutOfRangeException ex)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Error: {ex.Message}");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**What this example demonstrates**

| Feature | Code | Purpose |
|---------|------|---------|
| Auto‑implemented property | `public string FirstName { get; set; }` | Quick declaration when no extra logic is needed. |
| Private setter | `public string LastName { get; private set; }` | Readable publicly but only modifiable from inside the class. |
| Backing field + validation | `private int _age; …` | Encapsulate state and enforce rules. |
| Read‑only computed property | `public string FullName => $"{FirstName} {LastName}";` | Expose derived data without storing it separately. |

Run the program and you’ll see the console output reflecting each property’s behavior.
